<!--
    kuna alloca: a variable-length array under stack-clash protection.

    Source (gcc -O2 -fstack-clash-protection, the Ubuntu default):

        void use(char *p, int n);
        int vla(int n) { char buf[n]; use(buf, n); return buf[n/2]; }

        401155  movsxd rax,edi; mov rdx,rax; add rax,15
        401162  mov rsi,rax; and rsi,-0x1000      ; page part of the size
        401169  mov rcx,rsp; mov rbp,rsp; sub rcx,rsi
        401172  cmp rsp,rcx; je 40118c            ; guard
        401177  sub rsp,0x1000; or qword [rsp+0xff8],0; cmp rsp,rcx; jne 401177
        40118c  and eax,0xff0; sub rsp,rax        ; remainder
        401194  test rax,rax; jne 4011b8          ; probe the remainder too
        40119b  mov rdi,rsp; ... call use
        4011ae  movsx eax,byte [rsp+rax]

    The allocation printed as stack arithmetic around a probe loop
    (`while (v9 != v5) { ... *(unsigned long *)&v2[-8] = ... }`, then
    `use((long)v7 + v1,a0)`). Hex-Rays prints `alloca(size)` for the
    `__chkstk` form (hexx64.so 0x96240).

    Stage: P3 dataflow (RuleAlloca, RuleAllocaProbe) and the raw
    `sub rsp,reg` rewrite at ActionStart, option alloca off|on. Pass 1 (off)
    pins the bug, pass 2 (on, the default) the fix.
-->
